{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>That you eat nevelah and terefah.</b> Scripture speaks of the nevelah of a clean bird, which conveys tum'ah only at the time it is swallowed in the alimentary tract, and it teaches you here that it conveys tum'ah by its eating (and does not convey tum'ah by contact); and the terefah mentioned here was written only for midrash, as we learned: I might think the nevelah of an unclean bird conveys tum'ah in the alimentary tract — Scripture says 'terefah' — that which has a terefah in its kind, thereby excluding an unclean bird, which has no terefah in its kind (Sifra; Zevaḥim 70)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:53.971915883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}